From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: the Mac's display stays on while a video plays in the VM

What: the guest's display agent (omacvm-displays) sends
{"inhibit": ["Virtual-1", ...]} over org.omacvm.display: the outputs that
show a window whose app asks Wayland not to idle (zwp_idle_inhibit, as
mpv, Chromium 157+ and Firefox do while a video plays), without Hyprland
window rules, on a workspace that is shown, the session not locked; again
every 10 s, [] when it ends. QEMU then holds macOS's
PreventUserIdleDisplaySleep assertion "OmacVM: the VM is playing video"
(display only; the Mac still sleeps when the lid closes or someone picks
Sleep) while a listed output's Mac window can be seen (the sight
guest-pause uses: on screen, not covered, the screen neither locked nor
asleep, nobody else on the console), the VM runs and the word is under
30 s old. It is let go at once on [], at the lease's end, out of sight, a
lock, the channel closing, the VM stopping (QMP stop, shutdown) and before
the Mac sleeps; powerd's own timeout (45 s, Release, armed again every
10 s) backs a stuck main thread, and the assertion dies with QEMU. A line
with more than 16 names or anything but Virtual-N is ignored; older QEMUs
ignore the key, and an older guest sends none. qemu.log: the state at
start, each hold and release with why (at most 10 lines a minute), never
a word from the guest. OMACVM_VIDEO_AWAKE=0 leaves it out;
OMACVM_TEST_VIDEO_SEEN=1 (tests) counts a hidden test window as seen and
the test Mac's own lock as none: org.omacvm.test.lock stands for it.

Why: on battery macOS turned the display off after 2 min while the user
watched a video in the VM: a Mac player holds this assertion while it
plays, the VM's player only told the guest's compositor. ADR 0070.

Upstream: not sent (OmacVM's display channel).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-video-awake.sh (the rules, and the
wiring in the patched ui/cocoa.m at build time); src/app/guest/tests/
test_omacvm_displays.py (the agent's side). Applies after
omacvm-cocoa-guest-pause.patch, omacvm-cocoa-displays.patch and
omacvm-cocoa-drop.patch.

